<title>PERU: Peru's August iron output falls 20.0 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August iron output falls 20.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's iron output rose 20.0 percent to 190,997 tonnes in August, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Friday.</p>
<p>Production fell 19.9 percent to 2.123 million tonnes in the first eight months of the year, compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Output of Peruvian iron dropped 14.33 percent last year to 3.897 million tons compared with 4.549 million tons in 1994.</p>
<p>Peru's only iron miner is Chinese-owned Shougang Hierro Peru S.A, a former state-owned firm privatized in November 1992.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
